gyeo storm failed to find sunny skies at  the box office over its opening weekend  pulling in just thirteen point three  million dollars domestic against a  reported budget of over one hundred and  twenty million dollars the disaster  thriller starring Gerard Butler as a  scientist a task for fixing satellites  protecting the world from the  catastrophic effects of climate change  was the latest in a string of big-budget  flops in 2017 knocked down by a rocky  production and a chilly reception from  critics yeah I think we've established  that still there's a lot more to what  went wrong with Geo storm than just the  obvious here are the real reasons why  geo storm are flopped at the box office  stormy skies geo storm took a long time  to make its way to theaters the movie  was initially sold to Warner Brothers in  2014 with a release date set for March  of 2016 but then the release was bumped  to October of 2016 then to January of  2017 and finally its eventual October of  2017 release a lot happened in the  interim to her tear storms chances of  success including some production  hurdles that drove up the cost and  generated bad word-of-mouth sources say  that debut director Dean Devlin's first  coat was unwatchable  and despite weeks of post-production and  the numerous other test screenings  things didn't appear to get any better  it's gotta be a glitch Devlin reportedly  became overwhelmed with the movie scale  and struggled to get it ready on time so  with the director's blessing the studio  brought some mega producer Jerry  Bruckheimer to oversee some fifteen  million dollar in reshoots under  director Danny cannon and a screenwriter  lead to color Greta's the resuits  removed some characters looking to  better tie together the film's already  existing VFX sequences in a way that  made sense although reports say that the  film tested much better after the edits  the added time and cost and the bad  press that came with it didn't help been  there done that  another problem with Geo storm is that  disaster movies are hardly new in recent  years there have been a bevy of similar  projects like San Andreas and the  Deepwater Horizon to name a few and  while some have seen success for being  in on their own jokes like the sharknado  series geo storm was trying to be  completely serious and Fay  stiffer competition as a result Devlin  himself helped to crowd the field  further when he sets up the Independence  Day sequel resurgence the lackluster  reception of which signified the  audience fatigue with disaster movies  something geo storms disappointing  performance seems to confirm bad buzz  the audience's disinterest in turning  alfred geo storm was reflected in the  movie's social media conversation and  unless noted that most of the  conversation about the film online was  negative with the viewers comparing it  to films like Armageddon and The Day  After Tomorrow audiences have been  getting more discerning recently about  reboots and remakes and even though geo  storm isn't officially based on a past  property the fact that the movie Jaws so  heavily and what's come before without  appearing to offer much that's new was  enough to keep audiences at home the  film was also largely maligned with  critics the studio decided not to screen  the film for reviewers and even held  back on offering Thursday night  screenings to protect the movies  potential for a Friday night haul  however nothing could prevent the movie  from eventually landing in the tough  hands of critics who absolutely tore it  apart Geo storm currently sits at a  dismal 11 percent rating on Rotten  Tomatoes with critics knockin the movie  for being big dumb and boring that  certainly couldn't have helped draw in  anyone who was on the fence about seeing  it in the first place marketing mayhem  micah ting plays a huge part in the  chances of a movie success but if geo  storms PR campaign telegraphed anything  to viewers it was the fact that the film  was an absolute mess this was mainly  shown in the huge difference in tone  between the film's first and second  trailers the first geo storm trailer was  a somber affair but getting quiet and  eerie before underlining some terrifying  and deadly climate related events the  second though was more akin to a  disaster comedy using the same clips but  with much more lighthearted music and  some quips from Gerard Butler and his  co-stars to make the typhoons and  earthquakes seem more like a fun romp  than a catastrophic world-ending event  sorry but that literally had to fly in  from outer space a loss of this probably  came about thanks to the movie's  extensive reshoots but the fact that the  two trailers were selling entirely  different films wasn't a good sign for a  potential audience too soon geo storm  was also the victim of some pretty bad  timing  arriving in theaters as a nation was  still reeling from the effects of three  devastating hurricanes as well as deadly  earthquakes in Mexico and the  catastrophic flooding around the globe  with so much disaster happening in real  life it's easy to understand why  audiences might want to avoid seeing it  on the big screen geo storms marketers  recognize this and pour'd posters  featuring the movies old tagline braved  the storm replacing them with a new  tagline reading control the weather  control the world however that doesn't  appear to have been enough as the movie  underperformed in regions that have been  hit by the Hurricanes while there's some  debate as to how much outside events  affect the movie's box-office  performance the fact that so much of the  movie's plot was reminiscent of  real-life tragedies likely kept at least  some viewers away thanks for watching  click the loop icon to subscribe to our  youtube channel plus check out all this  cool stuff we know you're loved too  [Music]
 

